**What is claimed is:**

1. A fiber-optic pressure transducer for measuring pressure within a target environment, comprising:

a measuring head (10) configured to be positioned in fluid communication with the target environment, said measuring head (10) enclosing a pressure-sensitive diaphragm configured to deflect in response to variations in applied pressure;

a plurality of optical paths (30) operably coupled to said measuring head (10), the optical paths (30) configured to guide an input optical signal toward an interior surface of said pressure-sensitive diaphragm and to collect a reflected optical signal therefrom, wherein at least one parameter of the reflected optical signal varies as a function of the deflection of the diaphragm; and

a fastening device (20) mechanically coupled to said measuring head (10) and disposed peripherally about at least a portion of the optical paths (30), the fastening device (20) configured to secure the measuring head (10) in a fixed spatial position relative to the target environment while strain-relieving and maintaining the alignment of said optical paths (30) relative to the measuring head (10);

wherein the optical paths (30) extend longitudinally through the fastening device (20) into the measuring head (10) such that external mechanical forces exerted on the optical paths (30) are substantially decoupled from the measuring head (10).
